# dsh-kit — local artifacts
# No trailing slash: a POSIX link is a symlink, which git classifies as a file
# rather than a directory, so `node_modules/` would leave it untracked-but-visible
# and dirty the tree after a local development link.
node_modules
*.log
.DS_Store
profiles-web.bak/

# Per-run evidence, not source. Reports change on every run, so committing them would put
# a diff on every check and drown the changes that matter.
reports/

# Workspace-local application state: the taskboard ledger and similar per-checkout
# records. The kit ships the plugin, not your board.
.dsh/

# Local run artefacts that fall out of working on this machine: tool caches, the
# Playwright MCP session files, the launcher's pidfile, and the screenshots earlier
# sessions left at the root as evidence. Evidence belongs in reports/ (ignored above);
# none of this is source, and leaving it untracked made every `git status` noisy.
.cache/
.playwright-mcp/
server.pid
/*.png

# babysitter run journals (machine state, not kit source)
.a5c/

# Serena's per-project state (.serena/project.yml, symbol cache): created by the code-search
# pack's symbol server on first use, a property of the checkout rather than of the kit. The
# agent's tool calls are what write it, so it must not show up as a source change.
.serena/

# The desktop app's per-checkout state: attachments it copied in and task scratch
# files. The tracked .reasonix/*.json are the app's own metadata; these two trees
# are what working on this machine left behind, not kit source.
.reasonix/attachments/
.reasonix/tasks/

# Local analysis of the platform's usage export: a downloaded CSV, the scripts and the
# chart. It is this machine's billing data, not kit source.
.usage-analysis/
